<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Crisis</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mukden Incident</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1931">1931</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shenyang">Mukden</a> Incident was a staged explosion on a Japanese-owned railway near Mukden in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manchuria">Manchuria</a> in 1931. Officers of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kwantung-army">Kwantung Army</a> used it as a pretext to occupy Manchuria without authorisation from Tokyo. The incident led to the creation of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manchukuo">Manchukuo</a> and showed the army's growing power over the government of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/empire-of-japan">Empire of Japan</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mukden-incident.jpg" alt="Mukden Incident" width="320" height="256" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mukden_1931_japan_shenyang.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
